src/shim/privacy/data/tr_person_names.json carries, under "first_names", the
Turkish first names of Faker (https://github.com/joke2k/faker,
faker/providers/person/tr_TR), copyright Daniele Faraglia, under the MIT licence
in src/shim/privacy/data/LICENSE.faker, less entries that are ordinary words.
Its other lists ("team_first_names", the common first names Faker lacks;
"ambiguous_first_names"; "surnames"; "following_stopwords") were compiled by the
shim team from general knowledge, from no third-party dataset. They are lists of
facts, and no third-party licence applies to them.

src/shim/privacy/data/en_person_names.json carries, under "first_names", the
given names of the US Social Security Administration's national baby-name data
and of the US Census Bureau's 1990 first-name lists, and, under "surnames", the
US Census Bureau's 2010 surnames. These are works of the US federal government
and in the public domain (17 U.S.C. 105); "source" in the file names each
archive, its address and checksum, and the filter applied, and
scripts/person_names_en.py rebuilds both lists from the archives. Its other
lists ("team_first_names", "ambiguous_first_names", "ambiguous_surnames",
"not_names", "following_stopwords", "function_words", "name_suffixes",
"particles") were compiled by the shim team from general knowledge, from no
third-party dataset.
